GST Billing Utility v1.2.2 - Neon/Streamlit PostgreSQL Secrets Fix

REPLACE:
1. Replace the existing project db.py with db.py from this ZIP.

STREAMLIT CLOUD SECRETS:
Keep the existing Neon-style secrets format:

PGHOST = "your-neon-host"
PGDATABASE = "neondb"
PGUSER = "neondb_owner"
PGPASSWORD = "your-neon-password"
PGSSLMODE = "require"
PGCHANNELBINDING = "require"
GST_BILLING_ENV = "cloud"

DATABASE_URL is also supported, but is not required.

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT run any migration script.
- Do NOT recreate the Neon database.
- Do NOT delete or modify existing PostgreSQL tables.
- Do NOT upload real passwords to GitHub.
- In Cloud mode, if PostgreSQL credentials are missing or the connection fails, the app stops instead of falling back to SQLite.
- On a local machine, SQLite remains available when cloud mode is not enabled and PostgreSQL credentials are absent.

After replacing db.py:
1. Commit/push db.py to GitHub.
2. Confirm Streamlit Secrets contain the Neon variables above.
3. Reboot/redeploy the Streamlit app.
4. Verify existing Business, Clients, Items, Invoices and Users.
